---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Selected Work"
  description="Selected public projects by Eric Nolan across AI engineering, developer tooling, and practical software products."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Work</p>
      <h1>Selected public work</h1>
      <p class="lede">A small set of projects chosen for what they demonstrate, not a catalog of every repository.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell stack">
      <article class="card">
        <h2>Personal Memory Bank</h2>
        <p>Persistent project memory and governance for AI-assisted development. The interesting problem is not storing Markdown—it is managing authority, stale context, provenance, scope, handoffs, and deterministic enforcement over time.</p>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/unyieldingclaw-dev/personal-memory-bank">Repository →</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h2>AI Code Review Agent</h2>
        <p>A local AI-assisted review system built around specialized, isolated review perspectives, explicit failure behavior, structured outputs, and privacy-conscious inference.</p>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/unyieldingclaw-dev/ai-code-review-agent">Repository →</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <h2>PitLogic</h2>
        <p>A browser-based BBQ cook logging and analytics product with live device integration, alerts, predictions, testing, accessibility work, and static deployment.</p>
        <p><a href="https://github.com/unyieldingclaw-dev/pitlogic">Repository →</a></p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
